@lang en
-- Tests of ie-interpretation-time.l4: when an enactment comes into operation (sections 15 and 16, Schedule Pt 1 "commencement" and "midnight").
-- Expected values were written into NOTES.md section 2 from the text of ss 15(1), 16(1)-(4) before the code ran.
-- Reading aid: s 16(1) gives only a DAY (the date of passing); ss 16(2)-(4) give a MOMENT, the end of the day before a day.
-- The module stores that moment as "the end of D-1" and treats the end of one day and the start of the next as one point (assumption stated in the module header).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Helpers that build the facts about an enactment`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of enactment`
      s IS A `What an enactment says about its own commencement`
      d IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts about an enactment`
`the facts about an enactment of kind` k `that says` s `and was passed or made on` d MEANS
    `Facts about an enactment` WITH
        `its kind`                         IS k
        `what it says about commencement`  IS s
        `the day of its passing or making` IS d

`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` MEANS
    `the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))

`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026` MEANS
    `the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))

`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026` MEANS
    `the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))

§ `Worked case 1: an Act passed on 2026-03-10 that says nothing about commencement (s 16(1))`

-- the day: the date of its passing; s 15(1): the day the Bill is signed by the President
#ASSERT `the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT (`the commencement of` `an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`)'s `the provision that decides` EQUALS "section 16(1)"
-- the moment: s 16(1) names none, so asking for it refuses
#ASSERT REFUSED `the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` BECAUSE "section 16(1) names no moment within the date of passing"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of the enactment, as the Schedule defines the word` `an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`
-- by the end of that day it is in operation; by the end of the day before it is not
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 11)
-- throughout a whole day: the day before no, the day after yes, the day of passing is not answered; so neither is the first day on which it is in operation throughout
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 11)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the enactment` (`an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "the moment within a day at which the enactment comes into operation is not fixed by the text, so whether the whole of that day is in operation is not answered"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` `an Act that says nothing, passed on 10 March 2026` BECAUSE "the moment within a day at which the enactment comes into operation is not fixed by the text, so whether the whole of that day is in operation is not answered"

§ `Worked case 2: an Act expressed to come into operation on a day fixed later as 2026-06-01 (s 16(2))`

#ASSERT `the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT (`the commencement of` `an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`)'s `the provision that decides` EQUALS "section 16(2)"
-- the moment: the end of 2026-05-31
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT (`the commencement of the enactment, as the Schedule defines the word` `an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 31
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 5 30)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 5 31)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 6 2)
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` `an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
-- it is not in operation on the date of passing (the day is after the date of passing)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`an Act expressed to come into operation on 1 June 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 10)

§ `Worked case 3: a statutory instrument made on 2026-03-10 that says nothing about commencement (s 16(3))`

#ASSERT (`the commencement of` `a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`)'s `the provision that decides` EQUALS "section 16(3)"
-- the moment: the end of 2026-03-09, the day before the day of making
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 9
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2026 3 8)
-- so the whole of the day of making is in operation, but the whole of the day before is not
#ASSERT     `the enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026`) `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 9)
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` `a statutory instrument that says nothing, made on 10 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the first day on which a statutory instrument is in operation throughout` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10

§ `Statutory instruments expressed to come into operation on a particular day (s 16(4)), including a day before the day of making`

#ASSERT `the first day on which a statutory instrument is in operation throughout` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT (`the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 6 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))))'s `the provision that decides` EQUALS "section 16(4)"
-- a day before the day of making: the text says "whether the day is before or after the date of the making"
#ASSERT `the first day on which a statutory instrument is in operation throughout` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the enactment` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)))  `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)))  `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2026 2 28)
-- the same, for an Act whose particular day is before the date of its passing
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 3 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1

§ `Month ends, leap day and year end: the end of the day before the particular day`

-- 1 March 2024: the day before is the leap day
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2024 3 1))))'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
-- 1 March 2025: the day before is 28 February
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2025 3 1))))'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
-- 1 January 2026: the day before is 31 December 2025
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2026 1 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2025 11 3))))'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
-- a day that is a leap day itself
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 2024 2 29)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2024 1 5))))'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 28

§ `Cases the text does not answer: each refuses, naming why`

-- an Act expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained: no day exists to apply s 16(2) to
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10))) BECAUSE "the particular day on which the enactment is to come into operation has not been fixed or ascertained"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it is expressed to come into operation on a day not yet fixed or ascertained` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)))
-- the day of passing or making was not supplied: s 16(1) and s 16(3) need it
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `an Act of the Oireachtas` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the day of the passing or the making was not supplied"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statutory instrument` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` NOTHING) BECAUSE "the day of the passing or the making was not supplied"
-- a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force: s 15(1) defines the date of passing only for an Act of the Oireachtas, so s 16(1) cannot be applied when it is silent
#ASSERT REFUSED `the commencement of` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` `that says` `it says nothing about when it comes into operation` `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 1925 6 1))) BECAUSE "section 15(1) defines the date of passing only for an Act of the Oireachtas"
-- but when it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day, s 16(2) applies to "an Act"
#ASSERT `the first day on which the enactment is in operation throughout` (`the facts about an enactment of kind` `a statute of Saorstat Eireann continued in force` `that says` (`it is expressed to come into operation on a particular day` (YMD 1925 7 1)) `and was passed or made on` (JUST (YMD 1925 6 1))) EQUALS YMD 1925 7 1

§ `Section 15(1): the date of passing is the day the Bill is signed by the President`

#ASSERT `the date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas signed on` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS YMD 2026 3 10
#ASSERT `the date of the passing of an Act of the Oireachtas signed on` (YMD 2024 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29

§ `Section 1(2): this Act comes into operation on 1 January 2006 (and the date of its passing is endorsed in the text as 17 October 2005)`

#ASSERT `the day on which the enactment comes into operation, as the text names it` `the facts about this Act` EQUALS YMD 2006 1 1
#ASSERT (`the moment at which the enactment comes into operation` `the facts about this Act`)'s `the day it ends` EQUALS YMD 2005 12 31
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2005 12 31)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation throughout` (YMD 2006 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2005 12 30)
#ASSERT     `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2005 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the enactment` `the facts about this Act` `is in operation at the end of` (YMD 2005 10 17)
